* Sat Nov 09 2024 Qinyun Tan <qinyuntan@linux.alibaba.com> [5.10.134-16.5_rc1%%DIST%%]
- anolis: net/smc: upgrade smc dump header to version 2 (Wen Gu)
- anolis: net/smc: bring forward and fix rwwi CDC msg capture (Wen Gu)
- anolis: RDMA/erdma: Randomize the first allocated QPN (红海)
- anolis: net/smc: dump CDC msg in rwwi Tx and Rx path (Wen Gu)
- anolis: net/smc: dump CDC msg in Tx and Rx normal path (Wen Gu)
- anolis: net/smc: dump raw data in Tx and Rx path (Wen Gu)
- anolis: net/smc: implementation of dump data function (Wen Gu)
- anolis: net/smc: add netlink interface for dump_ndev operations (Wen Gu)
- anolis: net/smc: workaround for smc_pnet use with erdma OOB (Guangguan Wang)
- anolis: net/smc: introduce two sysctls for SMC-R memory limitation (Tony Lu)
- anolis: net/smc: always set sk_user_data for IPPROTO_SMC (D. Wythe)
- anolis: net/smc: support ipv4 mapped ipv6 addr client for smc-r v2 (Guangguan Wang)
- anolis: net/smc: Fix memleak in percpu ref (Kai Shen)
- anolis: RDMA/erdma: Support kernel-space scatter sq/rq buffer (红海)
- net/smc: introduce statistics for ringbufs usage of net namespace (Wen Gu)
- net/smc: introduce statistics for allocated ringbufs of link group (Wen Gu)
- net/smc: add sysctl for smc_limit_hs (D. Wythe)
- anolis: RDMA/erdma: Protect netdev reference in struct erdma_dev (红海)
- anolis: net/smc: fix for divide error in smc_dim (Guangguan Wang)
- anolis: net/smc: change min conn per lgr to 1 (Guangguan Wang)
- anolis: do not repeate stat rmb tx peer full when autosplit (Guangguan Wang)
- anolis: net/smc: introduce autosplit for smc (Guangguan Wang)
- anolis: net/smc: do not schedule credits_announce_work after link clearing (Guangguan Wang)
- anolis: RDMA/erdma: Update erdma driver (红海)
- anolis: net/smc: fix incorrect sndbuf setting (D. Wythe)
- anolis: net/smc: fix data_ready panic when listen sock shutdown (D. Wythe)
- anolis: net/smc: fix conflict IPPROTO_SMC from upstream (D. Wythe)
- anolis: net/smc: optimize smc reachability check when using erdma (Wen Gu)
- anolis: net/smc: restore the correspondence between sk_{snd|rcv}buf and sndbuf/RMB (Wen Gu)
- net/smc: avoid overwriting when adjusting sock bufsizes (Wen Gu)
- net/smc: change SMCR_RMBE_SIZES from 5 to 15 (Guangguan Wang)
- net/smc: set rmb's SG_MAX_SINGLE_ALLOC limitation only when CONFIG_ARCH_NO_SG_CHAIN is defined (Guangguan Wang)
- anolis: net/smc: use standalone filed to diff tcp_sock from smc_sock (D. Wythe)
- net/smc: fix neighbour and rtable leak in smc_ib_find_route() (Wen Gu)
- net/smc: make smc_hash_sk/smc_unhash_sk static (Zhengchao Shao)
- net/smc: reduce rtnl pressure in smc_pnet_create_pnetids_list() (Eric Dumazet)
- net: smc: fix spurious error message from __sock_release() (Dmitry Antipov)
- net/smc: fix missing byte order conversion in CLC handshake (Wen Gu)
- net/smc: return the right falback reason when prefix checks fail (Dust Li)
- net/smc: Use correct buffer sizes when switching between TCP and SMC (Gerd Bayer)
- net/smc: Fix setsockopt and sysctl to specify same buffer size again (Gerd Bayer)
- net/smc: Remove unused function declarations (Yue Haibing)
- mm/memory-failure: fix crash in split_huge_page_to_list from soft_offline_page (Miaohe Lin)
- anolis: priority oom: update nr_procs in de_thread (Xu Yu)
- hugetlb: pass head page to remove_hugetlb_page() (Naoya Horiguchi)
- drivers/perf: Fix ali_drw_pmu driver interrupt status clearing (Jing Zhang)
- arm64: kdump: defer the crashkernel reservation for platforms with no DMA memory zones (Baoquan He)
- arm64: kdump: do not map crashkernel region specifically (Baoquan He)
- arm64: kdump : take off the protection on crashkernel memory region (Baoquan He)
- arm64: kdump: Support crashkernel=X fall back to reserve region above DMA zones (Zhen Lei)
- arm64: kdump: Provide default size when crashkernel=Y,low is not specified (Zhen Lei)
- anolis: configs: disable CONFIG_RAS_CEC (Qiao Ma)
- bonding: 3ad: Print an error for unknown speeds (Ido Schimmel)
- bonding: 3ad: add support for 400G speed (Nikolay Aleksandrov)
- bonding: 3ad: add support for 200G speed (Nikolay Aleksandrov)
- bpf: Enforce W^X for bpf trampoline (Song Liu)
- anolis: uprobe: avoid out-of-bounds memory access of fetching args. (Qiao Ma)

